"""Reviewed snapshot of the RBT-002 decision-path census below the roots.

This is not a registry of what to enumerate. :func:`input_census.discover_decision_path`
decides membership from the roots; the RBT-002 enumeration then requires this
snapshot to equal the discovered census exactly, in both directions:

- every discovered type (other than the composer-facing input types, which
  ``coverage.FIELD_CLASSIFICATIONS`` classifies field by field) has one
  category here and exactly the discovered field names;
- every discovered non-root callable has exactly the discovered parameter
  names, in signature order;
- every discovered nested, local or private callable (correction R2) keeps its
  reviewed ``OWNER_INTERNAL``/``EXTERNAL`` classification and basis.

A type that gains or loses a field, a helper that gains or loses a parameter,
a newly reached owner and an owner that is no longer reached all fail the
enumeration until this snapshot is re-audited. It was generated from the
discovery, then each category and every newly discovered input was audited
(RBT-002 correction R1). Correction R2 added the 230 nested callables (2 local
functions, 40 lambdas, 188 generator expressions), each audited against its
recorded call sites. Classification semantics live in ``coverage``.
"""

